I've added slice 1 of #1184 and committed it as e85c68bc, titled "Part of #1184". Every config file yoyo loads now goes through the real TOML parser (the toml crate) first. If the file isn't valid TOML, yoyo prints the file, line and column, then exits before any model call. The readers still use the hand parser; later slices move them.

What I changed
• Dependency: added toml = "1" to Cargo.toml. Cargo resolved 1.1.2, not the 1.2.1 the task file mentioned.
• Check: config::toml_parse_error in src/config.rs returns a message like:
  ```
  error: .yoyo.toml:1:9: config file is not valid TOML: string values must be quoted, expected literal string
    |
  1 | model = m1
    |         ^^
  ```
  It then says that nothing ran and nothing was sent, and how to fix it. Columns count characters, not bytes, so lines with é or ✓ stay correct. The path and the quoted line are escaped before printing, since the file is untrusted text.
• Where it runs: first, every time the project, home or user config is loaded, which covers the REPL, -p, piped input, doctor, model, permissions and version -v. Those all exit 2.
• `config show` and `config get`: they read the file on their own, so they got the same check in src/commands_config.rs. config get exits 2, but config show exits 1 because its existing return type only allows that. In the REPL they print the error and the session keeps going.

Behaviour changes, all deliberate
• A value without quotes (model = m1) used to run as model m1. It's now refused.
• A key written twice used to keep the last value without saying so. It's now refused as "duplicate key".
• The inspection commands used to only warn about a malformed file and then show what the hand parser guessed. They now refuse. As a side effect, the old "config file is malformed" message can no longer fire for those cases; config_syntax.rs stays until the cleanup slice.

Checks
• I ran the built binary against a temp directory after cargo build finished. printf 'model = m1\n' > .yoyo.toml; yoyo -p hi --base-url http://127.0.0.1:9 exits 2 with the message above. Every other command listed refuses the same way. A duplicate key in ~/.yoyo.toml with no project file also exits 2, showing the full path.
• New tests: 8, in src/config_toml_tests.rs. They cover bare values, duplicate keys, the old malformed shapes, multi-byte columns and escaping. They also confirm that the valid shapes from #1174, #1177, #1178, #1180 and #1182, and the repo's own .yoyo.toml, still pass.
• Mutation check: I disabled the check and 5 of the 8 failed by name, then restored it (no leftover marker).
• Full suite: cargo test, clippy with -D warnings, fmt and module_size all pass. No existing test wrote an invalid config, so I didn't need to edit any fixtures.
• Docs: I rewrote the matching section of docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md for the new error.

I posted a scope comment on #1184 listing what's still open: the readers still hand-parse, writes still go through the line-based set_toml_key, and the hand parser, config_syntax.rs and the tomllib comparison test still need deleting after their cases move.
